I ran some mutation testing on the changed files. One surviving mutant seems relevant here:

<details>
<summary>Surviving mutant</summary>

`wallet/interfaces.cpp`: returning success on `MEMPOOL_REJECTED` survives. `CommitTransactionErrors` covers the rejection on `CWallet`, but the interface test `commit_transaction` (the path gui-qml#1008 uses) only covers `SUBMISSION_SKIPPED` and success.

```diff
-        return m_wallet->CommitTransaction(std::move(tx), /*replaces_txid=*/std::nullopt, /*comment=*/std::nullopt, /*comment_to=*/std::nullopt, messages);
+        auto result{m_wallet->CommitTransaction(std::move(tx), /*replaces_txid=*/std::nullopt, /*comment=*/std::nullopt, /*comment_to=*/std::nullopt, messages)};
+        // A transaction rejected by the mempool is still stored in the wallet and will be resubmitted later.
+        if (!result && result.error().code == node::TransactionError::MEMPOOL_REJECTED) return {};
+        return result;
```

</details>
